00:02:45,838 --> 00:02:47,520
1. Section Introduction.

47
00:02:47,726 --> 00:02:51,040
Let us begin with the production AI lifecycle framework.

48
00:02:51,246 --> 00:02:57,600
In a real enterprise environment, building an AI solution is not just about creating a model in a notebook.

49
00:02:57,870 --> 00:03:07,840
The model must move through a controlled pipeline that prepares data, trains the model, validates quality, serves predictions, monitors behavior, and improves over time.

50
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:09,828
This is why MLOps exists.

51
00:03:10,094 --> 00:03:14,320
It creates a predictable and repeatable path from experimentation to production.

52
00:03:14,638 --> 00:03:17,440
2. Core ideas and certification focus.

53
00:03:17,742 --> 00:03:24,000
The five major lifecycle stages are data preparation, model training, validation, serving, and monitoring.

54
00:03:24,302 --> 00:03:28,160
Data preparation converts raw information into model ready datasets.

55
00:03:28,622 --> 00:03:33,120
Model training uses GPU accelerated frameworks to learn patterns from data.

56
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:39,280
Validation checks accuracy, loss, safety, bias, and business thresholds before deployment.

57
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:43,280
Serving exposes the model through low latency production endpoints.

58
00:03:43,616 --> 00:03:47,296
Monitoring tracks both model behavior and infrastructure health.

59
00:03:47,566 --> 00:03:51,296
For certification, remember that NVIDIA stack is modular.

60
00:03:51,534 --> 00:03:56,976
Different tools handle different stages, but standardized APIs and containers help them work together.

61
00:03:57,294 --> 00:03:59,056
3. Explain the diagram.

62
00:03:59,342 --> 00:04:02,896
The diagram shows the life cycle as a loop rather than a straight line.

63
00:04:03,182 --> 00:04:05,216
The pipeline starts with data preparation.

64
00:04:05,486 --> 00:04:07,536
Clean data flows into model training.

65
00:04:07,758 --> 00:04:09,856
The trained model moves into validation.

66
00:04:10,158 --> 00:04:13,536
If the model passes quality gates, it is deployed for serving.

67
00:04:13,838 --> 00:04:19,216
Once it is serving users, monitoring collects performance, drift, and infrastructure telemetry.

68
00:04:19,438 --> 00:04:23,776
That monitoring feedback can trigger tuning, retraining, or redeployment.

69
00:04:24,078 --> 00:04:30,576
So the workflow is data, training, validation, serving, monitoring, and feedback into the next iteration.

